{
  "ruleId": "DED-NPS-EMPLOYER-GOVT",
  "_note": "The employer's contribution to the employee's account under the notified pension scheme, \"as does not exceed (a) 14%, where such contribution is made by the employer being the Central Government or the State Government\" \"of his salary in the tax year\" (s.124(1)(a), p.160); \"salary\" includes dearness allowance where the terms provide and excludes all other allowances and perquisites (s.124(13)(b), p.161) — base SALARY, the employer-pension salary. Survives the new regime (s.202(2)(a)(xii), p.227). TY 2026-27 only (D-129 C2a). rulebook DED-NPS-EMP-001(a), -003. Whether the contribution is salary first is OQ-14. The 1961 counterpart, s.80CCD(2), is unread (W-075d).",
